---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';

const path = '/guides';
const title = 'Shopify SMS operating guides';
const desc = 'Find a guide for the decision in front of you: permission, campaign cost, audience, timing, delivery or channel coordination.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} dateModified="2026-11-25" />
  <section class="py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="badge">Operating guides</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Shopify SMS operating guides</h1>
      <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl text-orange-950/80">{desc}</p>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl">Start with the unresolved decision, then carry its inputs and release conditions into the next step. These guides support an operating review; they do not certify legal compliance or promise campaign results.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify card">
      <h2>Establish who can receive the message</h2>
      <p>Use <a class="link" href="/guides/consent">SMS consent</a> to trace capture evidence, channel permission and revocation through imports and queued sends. Bring the disclosure version, capture source and current subscription state. The output should be an eligibility record you can inspect, including unresolved records held for review.</p>
      <p>The <a class="link" href="/guides/tcpa">TCPA basics page</a> introduces legal-review topics. Treat it as a starting list of questions for a qualified reviewer using current authority for your destinations and message categories, rather than approval to send.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify card">
      <h2>Price the intended operation</h2>
      <p>Open <a class="link" href="/guides/pricing">SMS pricing and contribution</a> when you need to compare invoices or evaluate a campaign. Bring destination mix, eligible audience, message composition, peak volume and written quote assumptions. Keep the cash forecast separate from incremental contribution; count discounts and refunds once and include the relevant product and operating costs.</p>
      <p>Then use the <a class="link" href="/apps">app directory</a> to investigate the tools that could own the job. Ask for evidence of the required workflow and current terms for your scenario before selecting a platform.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify card">
      <h2>Assign responsibility before comparing tools</h2>
      <p>For platform-specific investigation, open the reviews of <a class="link" href="/apps/postscript">Postscript</a>, <a class="link" href="/apps/attentive">Attentive</a>, <a class="link" href="/apps/sequenzy">Sequenzy</a> or <a class="link" href="/apps/klaviyo">Klaviyo</a>. These are navigation options, not a ranked shortlist or a prescribed stack. Write which system owns permission, audience updates, dispatch, replies and reporting; test the handoffs in the configuration you intend to use.</p>
      <p>Use <a class="link" href="/guides/campaign-restraint">campaign restraint</a> when the question is whether an additional promotional touch earns a slot. Bring the proposed reason to send and the other messages the same audience can receive. Leave with an explicit release or omission decision.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify card">
      <h2>Resolve timing, contact pressure and incentives separately</h2>
      <p>Use <a class="link" href="/guides/quiet-hours">quiet hours</a> to review dispatch windows, time-zone inputs and queued-message expiry. Bring a reviewed destination policy and test what happens when an offer expires while waiting. A sending window is not a universal permission rule.</p>
      <p>Return to <a class="link" href="/guides/campaign-restraint">campaign restraint</a> for total contact pressure; use <a class="link" href="/guides/offer-discipline">offer discipline</a> for incentive eligibility, combination behavior and checkout rehearsal. A valid time slot does not make another reminder useful, and a discount should address a defined purchase obstacle.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify card">
      <h2>Inspect audience membership</h2>
      <p>The <a class="link" href="/guides/segment-by-value">segment-by-value page</a> addresses audience selection. Bring inclusion and exclusion conditions, product interest and purchase records. Inspect members and nonmembers, distinguish missing data from low recorded spend, and recheck eligibility when the underlying events change. Spend alone should not decide permission or message relevance.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify card">
      <h2>Compare or replace a platform</h2>
      <p>Use <a class="link" href="/compare/postscript-vs-attentive">Postscript vs Attentive</a> and <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-omnisend">Klaviyo vs Omnisend</a> for pair-specific investigation. Bring the same audience, markets, workflow requirements and cost assumptions to both sides. Choose a test that can expose a missing control, rather than a universal winner.</p>
      <p>The <a class="link" href="/alternatives">alternatives directory</a> is a route into replacement planning. Inventory permission evidence, suppression history, queued messages and authoritative event sources before moving data. Define rollback and reconcile records before releasing promotions from the replacement system.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container pb-16">
    <div class="prose-shopify card">
      <h2>Find the missing handoff</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a class="link" href="/guides/list-growth">List growth:</a> use when a form or waitlist is collecting numbers without a clear capture promise. Bring the entry points and disclosure versions; trace one record through the sender handoff before expanding capture.</li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/guides/deliverability">Deliverability:</a> use when an expected text is missing. Bring message identifiers, event times and provider statuses; locate the break between eligibility, queue, acceptance and delivery reporting before retrying.</li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/guides/email-sms-coordination">Email and SMS coordination:</a> use when separate channels repeat an offer or disagree about customer state. Bring the combined journey and event ownership; rehearse a purchase or opt-out while a message waits.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Turn the reading into a release record</h2>
      <p>Record the campaign owner, audience purpose, permission source, exclusions, destination policy, offer expiry and failure response. Rehearse the relevant edge cases before release. If measuring incremental contribution, define a credible comparison and observation period in advance, retain required service communications, and report uncertainty alongside the result. A guide is useful when it resolves a specific operating question; reading every page is not a launch condition.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
